data.content:
Yes! MSTest v3+ supports **strongly-typed `DynamicData`** using tuples instead of `object[]`:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[DynamicData(nameof(TestData))]
public void Validate_ReturnsExpected(string input, bool expected)
{
    var result = Validator.IsValid(input);
    Assert.AreEqual(expected, result);
}

public static IEnumerable<(string Input, bool Expected)> TestData =>
[
    ("valid@email.com", true),
    ("invalid", false),
    ("", false),
];
```

**Key differences:**
- Return `IEnumerable<(string, bool)>` instead of `IEnumerable<object[]>`
- Use tuples `(...)` instead of arrays `[...]`
- Compile-time type checking — no more runtime `InvalidCastException` surprises

This requires **MSTest 3.4+** (the `MSTest.TestFramework` package). The test method parameters are automatically matched to the tuple elements by position.
